         <change when="2026-03-21T22:23:51-04:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/costasbala">Submit - Integration of BL 8, one new reading, one small correction.</change>
         <change when="2026-03-21T22:23:16-04:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/costasbala">Commit - I've integrated BL 8 in lin1 and lin7. In lin1 the papyrus appears to have γεγναμμενα, so more likely echoing γεγενημένα (cf. καλῶς γεγενῆσθαι is numerous documents); perhaps the scribe was thinking of γεγραμμένα at that moment. In lin14 a new reading: Η̣  ̣  ̣  ̣  ̣  ̣[ =&gt; Αὐρή̣λ̣ιο̣[ς. I wonder whether the subscriber in lin13 wrote his name not in the nominative but in the genitive instead, i.e. Αὐρήλιος Σαραπί[ω]νος.  </change>
